 "allGatesLocally": "81 of 81 passed on the final preparation (10 Nov). First pass: 72 green, 9 red. Taught the new adapters: performance-diagnostics (session comparison undoes the pause journal and dormant replacements first), hogwarts-dma-copies (later-adapter table), scalar-texture-descriptors and fallback-descriptor-scratch (melonx_descriptor_encoding_final undoes adapt_extra_array_dirty first), core667-fixes (QueueWriteToReadBarriers compared with the epoch pass undone; the buffer guard still checked first on the final method), bgc-fragmentation-guard (files_edited_later exemption, as bgc-keepalive), single-resource-bindings and bounded-binding-snapshots (the array fixtures' TextureStorage double gets AttachmentEpoch, moved by each of its counted barrier calls, so the array passes its storages each time as delivered). Load-dependent under three parallel gates, green alone and untouched by this Core: compute-switch-bindings (wall-clock comparison) and worker-library-share (render-thread creations within its time bound).",
